From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:56:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the ambient light
 sensor

The J604 ADT has /arm-io/aop/iop-aop-nub/als (harmony-db-version 3), and on
1.606 the AOP firmware announces the als service: the AOP core registers
als.N.auto under the AOP, unbound (no device tree node). The firmware
apple/aop-als-cal.bin is installed on the J604.

Enable the als child. aop_als (CONFIG_IIO_AOP_SENSOR_ALS=m in the official
configuration) then binds, reads the sensor's part name, sends it the
calibration and a 200 ms report interval, and registers an IIO light
device (in_illuminance) for brightness policy in user space. The part name
decides the report layout; a part the driver does not know (Redbird,
FireFish2 and CT817 are known) fails the probe with "Unknown sensor type",
and the AOP's other services are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 9f24fd68f8..a31895ac6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -731,6 +731,16 @@
 	apple,machine-kind = "MacBook Pro";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ambient light sensor: ADT /arm-io/aop/iop-aop-nub/als (harmony-db
+ * version 3); the J604 AOP firmware announces the service (als.N.auto on
+ * 1.606). The driver sends apple/aop-als-cal.bin, installed on the J604,
+ * to the sensor as its calibration.
+ */
+&aop_als {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &aop_dart {
 	status = "okay"; /* DTV-AUD-4 */
 };
